    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e2a218111671d3af61d734cb3bbf1d4b3060d58b4b3640440bcb72033c301f90",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Riemann's factorwise inversion reduces heterogeneous completed-zeta contributions to one parameterized kernel, the quantum-chaos source assigns prime powers formal orbit-action labels, and Connes supplies a general graph-diagonal mechanism by which transverse return maps produce trace weights. Together they define a trace-formula program, not an identification of primes with constructed classical orbits.",
